# The amplifier-side USB hub, and a bounded recovery for it enumerating empty.
#
# ITEM 25 ADDENDUM (2026-09-13 21:52): after a hot move the Atmel 4-port hub
# answered on the bus and none of its downstream ports did --
# `hub 1-2:1.0: hub_ext_port_status failed (err = -71)` -- so the audio adapter
# and the CH340 relay were both absent and item 25's BindsTo= recovery had
# nothing to recover onto. `authorized` 0 then 1 on the hub brought both back.
#
# ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device" IS LOAD-BEARING, AND IT IS ENV{}, NOT A BARE KEY.
# udev's match keys are KERNEL, SUBSYSTEM, DRIVER, ATTR{}, their *S variants,
# TAG{S}, ENV{}, CONST{}, TEST, PROGRAM and RESULT -- DEVTYPE is a device
# PROPERTY, so a bare `DEVTYPE==` is a parse error and the whole rule is
# dropped: no tag, no wants, and a recovery that silently never fires.
#
# Without the match at all this matches the hub's INTERFACE (1-2:1.0) as well as
# the device (1-2), and the instance name would then be a name
# with no `authorized` file -- the reset would run twice and the second one
# would fail on a path that cannot exist. The device is also the only node whose
# name is the bus id the reset script validates and walks children of.
#
# ATTR, NOT ATTRS. On the usb_device itself idVendor/idProduct are its own
# attributes; ATTRS would also walk up to the parent hubs and could match a
# chain that merely contains an Atmel device somewhere above it.
#
# NO ACTION=="add" ON THE TAG, for the reason spelled out in
# 90-wall-audio-adapter.rules: udev re-evaluates every rule on every event and a
# property this event did not set does not exist, so an add-only tag goes stale
# on the next non-add event and the unit stops being tracked. The WANTS is
# add-only on purpose though -- it is the event that starts a recovery, and
# re-running it on every change event is exactly the loop this must not become.
ACTION=="remove", GOTO="wall_usb_hub_end"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="03eb", ATTR{idProduct}=="0902", \
    TAG+="systemd"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="03eb", ATTR{idProduct}=="0902", \
    ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="wall-usb-hub-reset@$kernel.service"
LABEL="wall_usb_hub_end"
